<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:39:29 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Comeback kid: How did Brazil veteran-leader Lula upset Bolsonaro?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261026-comeback-kid-how-did-brazil-veteran-leader-lula-upset-bolsonaro</link><description>
Two days shy of his 81st birthday… Brazil’s Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva emerging as the comeback kid. Coming from behind in the polls after a bitter campaign where he often showed his age, Lula becoming the first candidate since Brazil’s return to democracy in the 1980s to win the presidential runoff after trailing in the first round. How did the Workers Party leader turn a 2-point-2 million vote deficit against the far-right's Flavio Bolsonaro into a 4-point-4 million vote win? Reminder that three short weeks ago, most races at the federal and state level broke the way of conservatives and the far-right? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83c7ae8c-d16e-11f1-a411-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T050657Z-1271320918-RC2OAOA8T6EG-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/83c7ae8c-d16e-11f1-a411-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T050657Z-1271320918-RC2OAOA8T6EG-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f4f3e8d8-d16d-11f1-a266-a93d017aa827</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:22:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: What does Lula's re-election mean for the Amazon?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-does-lula-s-re-election-mean-for-the-amazon</link><description>
Climate activists in Brazil are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04f1da5a-d160-11f1-81a2-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-173419-173609-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04f1da5a-d160-11f1-81a2-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-173419-173609-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0aac583a-d160-11f1-aeb8-a59138ab8242</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:18:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Leaders across Americas react to Brazil President Lula's re-election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-across-americas-react-to-brazil-president-lula-s-re-election</link><description>
​President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won Brazil's presidential election on Sunday (October 25), defeating right-wing ​Senator Flavio Bolsonaro in a runoff to secure a fourth non-consecutive term.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbe6938-d145-11f1-9537-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299151844900.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbe6938-d145-11f1-9537-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299151844900.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e54394ec-d15e-11f1-a23a-45ad538c3279</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:05:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Lula accustomed to negotiating tough bargains': Campaign promises collide with right-wing Congress</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-accustomed-to-negotiating-tough-bargains-campaign-promises-collide-with-right-wing-congress</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Christopher Sabatini, Director of Chatham House's Latin America Programme. Sabatini examines how Lula's campaign reinvention, youth mobilisation, and the changing dynamics of Bolsonarismo are reshaping Brazil's political landscape. By embracing social media, mobilising younger voters, and shifting attention from his historical achievements to the economic anxieties of ordinary Brazilians, Lula managed to transform the electoral contest. As Sabatini explains, voters were no longer satisfied with hearing about the past. They wanted an answer to a more immediate question: "What are you going to do for us now?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c2f2da2-d159-11f1-8aa9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-150453-151518-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c2f2da2-d159-11f1-8aa9-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-150453-151518-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a2bb9dfe-d159-11f1-825e-1da06aeafcfd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:54:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Down to Earth</category><title>Lula's re-election brings hope for the Amazon as deforestation drops to record low</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261026-lula-s-re-election-brings-hope-for-the-amazon-as-deforestation-drops-to-record-low</link><description>
Climate activists in Brazil and beyond are celebrating President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's election victory as good news for the Amazon rainforest. His last four years in power saw a record decrease in deforestation in the world's largest rainforest, appropriately nicknamed the planet's lungs. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6399ef56-d152-11f1-b866-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-TV-20241015-ENV-COL-AmazonForest-36EM6V7-en.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6399ef56-d152-11f1-b866-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-TV-20241015-ENV-COL-AmazonForest-36EM6V7-en.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17b078ba-d154-11f1-93ec-33705f0bf69b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:12:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valérie DEKIMPE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil's Lula reelected president in runoff vote: A look back at his career</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-reelected-president-in-runoff-vote-a-look-back-at-his-career</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term on Sunday (October 25), the country's electoral court said, in a shock result that defied polls.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01bf2c78-d14e-11f1-b175-4ba06036b7bc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:11:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms 2026: A history of gerrymandering</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-2026-a-history-of-gerrymandering</link><description>
What does a salamander have to do with US elections? Dating back centuries, gerrymandering continues to play a role in American elections today. Used more often by Republicans in the modern era of voting, Democrats have also resorted to the tactic in the past decade. But what is gerrymandering, and why is it called that? FRANCE 24's Tanishk Saha explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8ee3dee-d14a-11f1-9245-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumbnail-01-Gerrymandering.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a8ee3dee-d14a-11f1-9245-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumbnail-01-Gerrymandering.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dcbf3ec0-d14a-11f1-9017-e7dfd85b688e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:48:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Obama blasts Trump's 'chaos and cruelty' while campaigning for Democrats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-obama-blasts-trump-s-chaos-and-cruelty-while-campaigning-for-democrats</link><description>
Ten days out from the elections that will determine control of the closely divided Congress, Barack Obama took to the campaign trail to accuse the Republican president of corruption, deride his strategy for Iran and skewer the gilded aesthetic he has applied ‌to White House renovations. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa06634-d149-11f1-8d0a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b4f75ac.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7aa06634-d149-11f1-8d0a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2b4f75ac.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cca01f20-d143-11f1-b3e4-49483962c88f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:28:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula wins fourth term: What are the reactions in Brazil?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-wins-fourth-term-what-are-the-reactions-in-brazil</link><description>
Brazil's leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva was re-elected against all expectations on Sunday (October 25), but his conservative rival Flavio Bolsonaro refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to have the vote annulled. FRANCE 24's Jan Onoszko tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c5ea0e2-d145-11f1-aa19-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e357fa50.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c5ea0e2-d145-11f1-aa19-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e357fa50.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f4c9a80-d13b-11f1-a01f-2d8c0e72d7f9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:04:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bolsonaro's refusal to concede underscores ‘serious’ challenges to Brazil's democratic institutions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-refusal-to-concede-underscores-serious-challenges-to-brazil-s-democratic-institutions</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Dr Pedro Perfeito da Silva, Latin American specialist at the University of Exeter. For Dr Perfeito da Silva, Lula's stunning success reflects the convergence of digital organizing, grassroots mobilization, targeted socioeconomic appeals and an effective effort to mobilise opposition to the Bolsonaro political project. As he explains, Lula assembled a coalition that "not only energized his supporters but also attracted voters from groups that had been somewhat skeptical of the government in the first round."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a9e1cf2-d141-11f1-aa1e-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-130510-131145-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1a9e1cf2-d141-11f1-aa1e-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-130510-131145-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">20b851f2-d141-11f1-b53e-674a2aa97c8f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:53:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Lula wins Brazil election but faces uphill battle to govern</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-lula-wins-brazil-election-but-faces-uphill-battle-to-govern</link><description>
Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's narrow election victory on Sunday has dealt a blow to Brazil's far right, but deep political divisions remain. The newly re-elected president must tackle economic and security concerns at home while navigating international tensions with US President Donald Trump.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">74f669ea-d13a-11f1-987b-63085341f19e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:38:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd221fee-d13a-11f1-84ec-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4EJ8VV.jpg">© Miguel Schincariol, AFP</source><dc:creator>Anaëlle JONAH</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lula beats Bolsonaro in Brazil runoff: What does it mean for Donald Trump?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-lula-beats-bolsonaro-in-brazil-runoff-what-does-it-mean-for-donald-trump</link><description>
Lula defeated on Sunday (October 25) Flavio Bolsonaro in Brazil’s presidential election. But rather than conceding, Bolsonaro called for the result to be annulled. As the US midterms approach, the result raises questions about Trump’s influence and how his political allies respond when voters reject them. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Douglas Herbert, gives us his analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/407c3b70-d0e7-11f1-af1e-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277709264055-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/407c3b70-d0e7-11f1-af1e-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26277709264055-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e65a7cde-d126-11f1-bca0-8f22189af98a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:50:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Trump's gains among Latino voters in Texas at risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-us-midterms-trump-s-gains-among-latino-voters-in-texas-at-risk</link><description>
Latino voters shifted toward Trump two years ago, helping him return to the White House with a Republican-controlled Congress. Now, many are souring on the US president and his party. FRANCE 24's team reports from the Rio Grande Valley.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c59e456-d128-11f1-ab5d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-85a53c06.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9c59e456-d128-11f1-ab5d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-85a53c06.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0ddb751e-d128-11f1-918a-ff50aa936331</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:42:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: What challenges await Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-what-challenges-await-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). He will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b1f50c-d0d7-11f1-9469-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/0498b5dbd26c81f0b76b2b0960050a2224c1a10b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b1f50c-d0d7-11f1-9469-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/0498b5dbd26c81f0b76b2b0960050a2224c1a10b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e5a427e-d11b-11f1-b144-ef6f354a7560</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:46:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil's Lula wins historic fourth term</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-wins-historic-fourth-term</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 26). The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ceee314c-d119-11f1-9027-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090215-090410-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ceee314c-d119-11f1-9027-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-090215-090410-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d401da3a-d119-11f1-bbcb-133043b7213b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:44:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil's Lula seals re-election in surprise win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-lula-seals-re-election-in-surprise-win</link><description>
Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won an unprecedented fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday (October 25). The far-right candidate and son of former President Jair Bolsonaro has refused to accept the results and said he would seek to annul the vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65bc2598-d11f-11f1-8fc5-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/title-4.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65bc2598-d11f-11f1-8fc5-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/title-4.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a151a30-d11c-11f1-ab18-cb64ae6d33fe</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:33:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Congratulations!’: World leaders hail Lula’s election victory in Brazil</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-congratulations-world-leaders-hail-lula-s-election-victory-in-brazil</link><description>
The international community on Monday congratulated Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva after his stunning re-election in a runoff with right-wing candidate Flavio Bolsonaro. The region's left-leaning leaders were quick to react as Brazil staved off a conservative wave in many countries while Europeans, such as Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez, celebrated a "progressive comeback".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8712ae4-d0f1-11f1-829d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T035757Z-1722584206-RC2RAOA2Q30I-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8712ae4-d0f1-11f1-829d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T035757Z-1722584206-RC2RAOA2Q30I-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e69002a-d118-11f1-bcc0-678a93ac0221</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:31:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8712ae4-d0f1-11f1-829d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T035757Z-1722584206-RC2RAOA2Q30I-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg">© Alexandre Meneghini, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[Lula's 'extraordinary victory' faces growing middle class, deeply-entrenched bolsonarismo & Big Tech]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lula-s-extraordinary-victory-faces-growing-middle-class-deeply-entrenched-bolsonarismo-big-tech</link><description>
Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Dr Felipe Krause, Political Scientist, former Diplomat and Departmental Lecturer in Latin American Studies at the Oxford School of Global and Area Studies.  Beneath Lula's electoral triumph lies a more complex political reality: the Brazilian hard right has consolidated its influence across state governments and legislative institutions, raising fundamental questions about the balance of power and the future of progressive governance. Lula will be focusing more on "working to keep things from eroding" rather than advancing his progressive agenda, explains Dr. Krause. 'There is more need for economic measures that support the growing middle class."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/690b2716-d116-11f1-a852-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-080414-081316-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/690b2716-d116-11f1-a852-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-080414-081316-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e4ba674-d116-11f1-8b51-cd336633b4fd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:41:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What challenges await Brazil's Lula in his fourth term as president?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-what-challenges-await-brazil-s-lula-in-his-fourth-term-as-president</link><description>
President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will have to wrestle with a divided Brazil, an unfriendly Congress, feeble public finances and a Donald Trump-shaped menace during his unprecedented fourth term.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b1f50c-d0d7-11f1-9469-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/0498b5dbd26c81f0b76b2b0960050a2224c1a10b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b1f50c-d0d7-11f1-9469-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/0498b5dbd26c81f0b76b2b0960050a2224c1a10b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">942699b0-d0d7-11f1-9531-8353dbbe79d5</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:52:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92b1f50c-d0d7-11f1-9469-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/0498b5dbd26c81f0b76b2b0960050a2224c1a10b.jpg">© Silvio Avila, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Lula beats odds and seals re-election, rival Bolsonaro demands annulment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261026-brazil-s-president-lula-da-silva-beats-flavio-bolsonaro-to-win-re-election</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, nearly 81 years old, clinched a fourth term in a tight runoff against Flavio Bolsonaro on Sunday. The leftist leader won 51.7% of the vote, compared to 48.2% for the son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, official results showed. Bolsonaro has refused to accept the loss and said he would seek to annul the vote.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d08bd462-d0d0-11f1-ab21-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-25T220534Z-34599975-RC2KAOAZJ6YN-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d08bd462-d0d0-11f1-ab21-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-25T220534Z-34599975-RC2KAOAZJ6YN-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a6d2942-d0d3-11f1-b9ab-8d756989d7e3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:23:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d08bd462-d0d0-11f1-ab21-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-25T220534Z-34599975-RC2KAOAZJ6YN-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg">© Tuane Fernandes, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Brazil presidential election: Lula's late surge</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261025-lula-s-legacy-flavio-s-future</link><description>
It's a coin-flip election in Brazil, with little separating the country's left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro. The results of the run-off vote will become clear in a few hours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc50934-d0a5-11f1-89fc-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-10-25-at-19-49-17-1.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc50934-d0a5-11f1-89fc-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-10-25-at-19-49-17-1.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">feacf2ca-d09b-11f1-8b8d-779ad7a451b4</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:00:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Opposition leader Machado returns to Venezuela after 10 months in exile</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-opposition-leader-machado-returns-to-venezuela-after-10-months-in-exile</link><description>
Venezuelan opposition leader Maria Corina Machado announced on Sunday that she has returned to her homeland following almost a year in exile, after covertly leaving Venezuela in late 2025 to receive the Nobel Peace Prize. She returns as doubts about her country’s democratic future and the role of the US are growing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a71cd552-d096-11f1-a147-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4DM8NQ-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a71cd552-d096-11f1-a147-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4DM8NQ-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cbff47b4-d092-11f1-a65d-0bb228e421f6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:10:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a71cd552-d096-11f1-a147-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4DM8NQ-1.jpg">© Handout, Vente Venezuela Press Office / AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Presidential runoff under way in Brazil</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/presidential-runoff-under-way-in-brazil</link><description>
Brazil is also heading to the polls today for a run-off vote that will decide who leads the country. The race is on a knife edge between incumbent left-wing President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and right-wing Senator Flávio Bolsonaro. The son of former president Jair Bolsonaro, Flávio scored a major upset in the first round earlier this month, taking the lead in the vote. The campaign has been dominated by corruption scandals, economic difficulties and allegations of US interference, which Washington has denied. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko reports the latest from Rio de Janeiro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8da640e8-d07a-11f1-9394-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-140536-140901-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8da640e8-d07a-11f1-9394-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-140536-140901-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93359d74-d07a-11f1-9a02-83411c56a6a1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:52:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Lula thanks voters for his victory, Bolsonaro does not recognise the results</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonaro</link><description>
It is the first time in Brazil's history since the return of democracy in the country that a candidate who lost in the first round managed to come back and win in the runoff. The left-wing president Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva obtained 51.7% of the votes, compared with 48.2% won by right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb7ae58-d0dc-11f1-a64c-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T012154Z-495985530-RC2PAOAKLO54-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb7ae58-d0dc-11f1-a64c-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T012154Z-495985530-RC2PAOAKLO54-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">635aedf6-ced7-11f1-9289-95da0497d4a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:46:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb7ae58-d0dc-11f1-a64c-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T012154Z-495985530-RC2PAOAKLO54-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg">© Brian Snyder, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Polls open in Brazil presidential runoff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption. France 24 Jan Onoszko telles us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f689cca0-d067-11f1-911d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-120157-120549-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f689cca0-d067-11f1-911d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-120157-120549-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fbd61f10-d067-11f1-8c27-3df80effe4d1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:40:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Obama hits campaign trail for democrats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats</link><description>
With less than two weeks to go before the US midterm elections, former President Barack Obama has hit the campaign trail, rallying support for Democratic candidates in the key states of Michigan and Ohio. He criticised the Trump administration, blaming the White House for rising living costs, a major concern for voters. Democrats are hoping to regain control of Congress, with polls showing several closely contested races. Ophelie Jacobson has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6c5f842-d067-11f1-838f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-111149-111339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6c5f842-d067-11f1-838f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-111149-111339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac035e62-d067-11f1-bea8-35f7b887b3db</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:36:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What to know as Brazilians choose between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro in tense presidential run-off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff</link><description>
Brazilians are set on Sunday to choose between leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro in the run-off vote of a deeply polarizing presidential election, and one which will determine whether the US significantly expands its growing influence in Latin America.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b39c072-cf58-11f1-9e7d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/1ae128fbd285ad0911fa3c7032f2b685dafb9fee.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b39c072-cf58-11f1-9e7d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/1ae128fbd285ad0911fa3c7032f2b685dafb9fee.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6afa98e-d037-11f1-89cb-0d5e7772cd90</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:05:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b39c072-cf58-11f1-9e7d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/1ae128fbd285ad0911fa3c7032f2b685dafb9fee.jpg">© Andre Coelho, EFE</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US seeks to topple Cuba's government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-seeks-to-topple-cuba-s-government</link><description>
And now, in a rather surprising development, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is directly urging Cubans to cooperate with the CIA. Havana has responded by mocking what it calls the Trump administration’s “desperation”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/774541f4-cf9f-11f1-b1e6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-132342-132536-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/774541f4-cf9f-11f1-b1e6-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-132342-132536-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c6201ea-cf9f-11f1-8024-3b4cfdd7f55b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:43:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump challenges Alaska Senate trace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-challenges-alaska-senate-trace</link><description>
With the US midterm elections less than two weeks away, concerns are growing over whether President Donald Trump would accept a major Republican defeat. Trump has called for legal action to block the certification of Alaska’s Senate race if Republican incumbent Dan Sullivan loses to his Democratic challenger, Mary Peltola, arguing that another candidate with the same name on the ballot could confuse voters. Our Washington correspondent Fraser Jackson has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2432c252-cf9f-11f1-b529-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-132110-132313-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2432c252-cf9f-11f1-b529-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-132110-132313-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">29722384-cf9f-11f1-a7ba-6baa24d1d2ae</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:42:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump administration sues to block possible Democratic win in Alaska Senate race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261024-trump-administration-sues-to-block-possible-democratic-win-in-alaska-senate-race</link><description>
US President Donald Trump said Friday that he had instructed his administration to file a lawsuit to block the certification of the US Senate race in Alaska if Republican Senator Dan Sullivan loses, arguing that voters would be confused because two Republicans on the ballot have similar names. The legal battle is ramping up questions over whether Trump will accept a potential midterms defeat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daf057b4-cf9c-11f1-9be0-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294747292303.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daf057b4-cf9c-11f1-9be0-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294747292303.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aed74296-cf9c-11f1-a10b-5522b2e59ad4</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:40:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/daf057b4-cf9c-11f1-9be0-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294747292303.jpg">© Haven Daley, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
